  "articleSummary": "**Summary:**\n\n* **Core Thesis:** The primary security threat of AI agents is not a sci-fi singularity, but the compounding multiplication of agent endurance and orchestrated breadth, weaponized via stolen cloud credentials (\"LLMjacking\") where the victim pays for the attacker's compute.\n* **Key Technologies & Concepts:** Multi-hour autonomous agents (citing METR benchmarks), multi-agent orchestrators (referencing Anthropic's disclosure of GTG-1002), LLMjacking (unauthorized consumption of victim cloud resources), and the probabilistic failure of linear defense against non-linear swarm economics.\n* **Tone & Framing:** Written as a pragmatic, slightly cynical analytical warning, the article uses the *Terminator* (\"absolutely will not stop\") as a recurring framing device, updating the metaphor from an unstoppable physical chassis to an unstoppable billing meter.\n* **Intended Audience:** Software engineering teams, cloud security professionals, and skeptics who view current agentic AI threats as overblown hype.",
